==Old English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ʃi:r/|lang=ang}}, {{SAMPA|/Si:r/|lang=ang}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gem|ang}} ''*skizo''.  Cognate with Old High German {{term|scira|scīra|lang=goh}}, Welsh {{term|sir|lang=cy}}.

====Noun====
{{infl|ang|noun|head=scīr}}

# a [[shire]], consisting of a number of [[hundred]]s or [[wapentake]]s, ruled jointly by an [[alderman]] and a [[sheriff]]

====Derived terms====
* [[scirgerefa|scīrġerēfa]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|gem|ang}} ''*skeira-''.  Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|skire|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{term|skir|skīr|lang=osx}} (Dutch {{term|schier||white, grey|lang=nl}}, German {{term|schier||pure|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|skirr|skírr|lang=non}} (Swedish {{term|skir|lang=sv}}), Gothic {{term|𐍃𐌺𐌴𐌹𐍂𐍃|sc=Goth|lang=got}}  Related to {{term|scinan|lang=ang}}.

====Adjective====
{{infl|ang|adjective|head=scīr}}

# [[bright]], [[shining]]
# [[clear]], [[pure]]

